{"name":"Demon Princess","hex":"#d2144b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"demon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evil supernatural being.\nAn evil being resident in or working for Hell; a devil. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\n A false god or idol; a Satanic divinity. \n A very wicked or malevolent person; also  a mischievous person, especially a child. \nA source (especially personified) of great evil or wickedness; a destructive feeling or character flaw.","An evil being resident in or working for Hell; a devil. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Acronym of distinct electron motion particle: a quasiparticle, a type of massless neutral electron excitation associated with superconductivity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demon"},{"term":"princess","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female member of a royal family other than a queen, especially a daughter or granddaughter of a monarch. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A woman or girl who excels in a given field or class."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/princess"}],"entries":[{"title":"Demon","blocks":[{"text":"A demon is an evil or malevolent supernatural entity, though they can be benevolent too. Historically, belief in demons, or stories about demons, occurs in folklore, mythology, religion, occultism, and literature; these beliefs are reflected in media including fiction, comics, film, television, and video games. Belief in demons probably goes back to the Paleolithic age, stemming from humanity's fear of the unknown, the strange and the horrific. In ancient Near Eastern religions and in the Abrahamic religions, including early Judaism and ancient-medieval Christian demonology, a demon is considered a harmful spiritual entity that may cause demonic possession, calling for an exorcism. Large portions of Jewish demonology, a key influence on Christianity and Islam, originated from a later form of Zoroastrianism, and was transferred to Judaism during the Persian era."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/PazuzuDemonAssyria1stMillenniumBCE_no_CGI_dropshadow_-_gradient_based_on.jpg/330px-PazuzuDemonAssyria1stMillenniumBCE_no_CGI_dropshadow_-_gradient_based_on.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demon"},{"title":"Princess","blocks":[{"text":"Princess is a title used by a female member of a regnant monarch's family or by a female ruler of a principality. The male equivalent is a prince. Most often, the term has been used for the consort of a prince, or for the daughter of a monarch. A crown princess can be the heir apparent to the throne or the spouse of the heir apparent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg/330px-Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Mephistopheles2.jpg/500px-Mephistopheles2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Mephistopheles2.jpg/1280px-Mephistopheles2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Mephistopheles2.jpg/500px-Mephistopheles2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mephistopheles (a medieval demon from German folklore) flying over Wittenberg, in a lithograph by Eugène Delacroix.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMephistopheles2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Ram-headed_demon_gradient_background.jpg/330px-Ram-headed_demon_gradient_background.jpg?utm_sour